+	/* qos_obw is the user's MEASURED upload (honest decimal kbps). Shape the
+	 * egress aggregate at ~90% so the ROUTER owns the bottleneck and the ISP's
+	 * upstream buffer stays drained - a shaper at 100% of measured leaves the
+	 * standing queue at the ISP and defeats QoS. This is the SAME 10% headroom
+	 * already applied to the ingress policer below (prate = ibw - ibw/10) and to
+	 * both cake directions. Applied ONCE here so every egress consumer inherits
+	 * it: per-class calc(obw,ceil/rate), the qid 0 / qid 6 caps, and the port
+	 * shaper. Do NOT also bake headroom into the page or a second engine site. */
+	obw -= obw / 10;
